# Backend Laravel

- Use Laravel 13 conventions and PHP 8.4 syntax.
- Keep API endpoints in `backend/routes/api.php`; they are exposed under `/api`.
- Return API responses as JSON and cover new endpoints with feature tests in `backend/tests/Feature`.
- Keep CORS settings in `backend/config/cors.php`; allowed frontend origins come from `FRONTEND_URL`.
- Prefer Form Requests, Resources, Actions/services, and feature tests once business logic grows beyond simple routes.
- Do not put business logic in controllers if it becomes reusable or stateful.
- After backend changes, run the smallest relevant check first:
  - `cd backend && php artisan test --filter=<TestName>`
  - `cd backend && vendor/bin/pint --test`
  - `cd backend && vendor/bin/phpstan analyse --no-progress`
- Docker/Makefile equivalents:
  - `make test`
  - `make pint`
  - `make stan`
  - `make backend-lint`
- If changing `backend/composer.json`, keep `backend/composer.lock` in sync and avoid unrelated dependency updates.
